From f95e85f20e14b27ee0dcc57075473502dd25cfe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:57:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-110: Tab walks the values, Enter stays in the
 field; the page events' right-click menu (0.110.0)

WPF's property grid: Tab goes from one property's value to the next, and Enter
writes the value and leaves you in the field. Here Tab also stopped on the
property marker, the colour well and its arrow (and on every event row besides
its field), and Enter left the field -- a click to go on. Now only the values
are Tab stops, and Enter writes once and stays with the value selected (numbers,
Caption, Font.Name, the page's JS events). The page's JS events get the
component events' right-click menu: jump to the code / Reset (takes the binding out).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (the 13 Tab stops all values, no event row; Left / Caption / Font.Name /
click: Enter -> focus kept, value selected, sent once; a page event's menu:
jump = openJsEvent, Reset = the binding out, both off on an empty one).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
